docs {
  # CreditAPI end-to-end tests

  Runs against the real server with the fake Claude and Cursor CLIs
  (`bin/fakeclaude`, `bin/fakecursor`), so no account is needed. Start the stack
  with `make e2e` (uses `.env.bruno`), then run this collection from the Bruno app
  with the `local` environment or with `make bruno`. `make e2e-ci` does both
  headless.

  The first folder resets the server (signs the first Claude subscription out and
  removes subscriptions left by an earlier run), so the collection can be re-run
  against the same stack. The fake CLIs react to `[fake:...]` directives in
  prompts; see `src/tests/support/fakecore/core.go`.
}
